|From 6b1d0c1f7a2e4f9c8d3b5a6e7f8091a2b3c4d5e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
|From: Felipe De Bene <benfelip@amazon.com>
|Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:20:00 +0000
|Subject: Haiku: add the haiku-aarch64 target
|
|There was no arm64 entry, so ./config on arm64 Haiku (uname -m "arm64")
|matched the '.*-.*-haiku' catch-all and configured haiku-x86: 32-bit
|bignum limbs (BN_LLONG, "bn(64,32)") on a 64-bit CPU, and, with the
|recipe's no-asm, none of the ARMv8 AES, PMULL, SHA or bignum assembly.
|
|haiku-aarch64 takes linux-aarch64's asm_arch and linux64 perlasm flavour
|(plain GNU-as ELF) on haiku-common. bn_ops is SIXTY_FOUR_BIT_LONG alone,
|as for haiku-x86_64: linux-aarch64's RC4_CHAR would also change the
|public RC4_KEY layout, and buys nothing here.
|
|armcap.c detects the crypto extensions with getauxval() where the
|platform has one. DeBeOS's libroot answers AT_HWCAP/AT_HWCAP2 in the
|Linux bit layout from the ID registers EL0 cannot read. It leaves
|HWCAP_CPUID and HWCAP_SVE clear, so OpenSSL neither executes an EL0 MRS
|of MIDR_EL1 nor turns on SVE paths the kernel has not advertised. The
|include is unconditional on Haiku: the SIGILL-probe fallback would
|probe SVE successfully and enable it.
|
|os-dep/haiku.h, which haiku-common force-includes into every compile,
|is skipped under __ASSEMBLER__. The aarch64 perlasm output is .S, run
|through the preprocessor, and the C declarations from <sys/select.h>
|were assembler errors (x86_64's perlasm emits plain .s, so it never
|hit this).
|---
|diff --git a/Configurations/50-haiku.conf b/Configurations/50-haiku.conf
|--- a/Configurations/50-haiku.conf
|+++ b/Configurations/50-haiku.conf
--------------------------
